e seven will be and we  continue filling it out we'll figure out  where the eight is by going up into the  right and the nine will also be up into  the right of eight as you get a few of  these in you can also fill them out just  by knowing that the sum of each row or  diagonal or column will be 15 so now we  have a Magic Square where every row and  column and diagonal sums up to 15 and  those are the only sets of three numbers  that add up to 15 so let's try and solve  the game so what we'll do is we'll  imagine when Alice picks a number we'll  visualize it on this 3x3 grid and we'll  mark her spot with an X so let's say she  picked 2/5 we put an X in the center  whichever number Bob picks if he picks  an 8 we'll put an O in that square so  having a sum of 15 means getting a three  in a row because the only way to get 15  is to have one of the rows columns or  diagonal and that's the insight this  game is exactly like tic-tac-toe  so wherever Alice goes and Bob's go  we're alternately picking X as a No both  players trying to get three in a row  since tic-tac-toe ends in a draw this  game also ends in a draw did you solve  the puzzle  I hope you liked this video please  subscribe to my channel you can support  me on patreon for exclusive rewards  catch me on my blog mynheer decisions on  Twitter at pressure Walker and you can  get my books listed on my website
 

